[SIZE="4"][B]Developer API[/B][/SIZE]

Shopping List 0.16.3 includes public API version 1. Other addons can add item links or plain item names to an active shopping list without accessing Shopping List's saved variables or internal UI objects.

[B]Load order[/B]

Add Shopping List to your addon manifest as an optional dependency:

[CODE]## OptionalDependsOn: GravvyShoppingList[/CODE]

Use [CODE]## DependsOn: GravvyShoppingList[/CODE] instead if your addon cannot function without it. Both the manifest dependency name and Lua API namespace use [CODE]GravvyShoppingList[/CODE]. Check that the API is available after your addon loads:

[CODE]local api = GravvyShoppingList and GravvyShoppingList.API
if not api or api:GetVersion() < 1 then
    return
end[/CODE]

[B]Add an item[/B]

[CODE]local success, itemIdOrError = api:AddItem(
    itemLinkOrName,
    quantity,
    options
)[/CODE]

[LIST]
[*][B]itemLinkOrName[/B] - A complete ESO item link or a non-empty plain item name.
[*][B]quantity[/B] - A whole number from 1 through 1,000,000.
[*][B]options[/B] - An optional table containing listId, listName, note, or silent.
[/LIST]

Use either [B]listId[/B] or [B]listName[/B], not both. If neither is supplied, Shopping List uses the player's currently selected list. List-name matching is case-insensitive, and targeting another list does not change the player's selected list.

[CODE]local success, result = api:AddItem(itemLink, 5)
if success then
    local newItemId = result
else
    local errorCode = result
end[/CODE]

You can target a named list and include a note:

[CODE]local success, result = api:AddItem("Rubedite Ingot", 200, {
    listName = "Crafting Materials",
    note = "Needed for the next equipment set",
})[/CODE]

Set [CODE]silent = true[/CODE] if Shopping List should not update its own status line. API calls never open the Shopping List window or item editor and never write to chat.

Complete item links are preferred. They allow Shopping List to initialize the exact item identity plus set, trait, quality, level, and Champion Point matching information. Plain names create unrestricted name-based entries. Every API call creates a separate entry so similarly named items with different traits or levels are never merged accidentally.

[B]Discover active lists[/B]

[CODE]local lists, errorCode = api:GetLists()
if lists then
    for _, list in ipairs(lists) do
        d(string.format("%d: %s", list.id, list.name))
    end
end[/CODE]

GetLists returns fresh copies containing only [CODE]id[/CODE] and [CODE]name[/CODE]. Archived lists are not included, and changing a returned table does not alter Shopping List data.

[B]API and error versions[/B]

[CODE]local apiVersion = api:GetVersion() -- 1[/CODE]

The API version is separate from the Shopping List addon version. AddItem returns [CODE]true, itemId[/CODE] on success or [CODE]false, errorCode[/CODE] on failure. GetLists returns [CODE]lists[/CODE] on success or [CODE]nil, errorCode[/CODE] before initialization.

[LIST]
[*][CODE]NOT_READY[/CODE] - Shopping List has not finished initializing.
[*][CODE]INVALID_ITEM[/CODE] - The value is empty, malformed, or not an item link.
[*][CODE]INVALID_QUANTITY[/CODE] - Quantity is outside the supported range or is not a whole number.
[*][CODE]INVALID_OPTIONS[/CODE] - The options table or a supported option is invalid.
[*][CODE]LIST_NOT_FOUND[/CODE] - The requested active list does not exist.
[/LIST]

Error constants are available without hard-coding their values:

[CODE]if not success and result == api.ERROR.LIST_NOT_FOUND then
    -- Ask the player to choose another list.
end[/CODE]

Only [CODE]GravvyShoppingList.API[/CODE] is public. Integrations should not access [CODE]GravvyShoppingList.data[/CODE], Shopping List saved variables, or internal UI objects. Full technical documentation is included with the addon in DeveloperAPI.txt.
